; --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; squaretable.asm: The table of squares and the back buffer
;
; The kickoff builds the table of squares (n² for n = 0-255: the low bytes at $BE00, the high bytes at $BF00) where
; the tape carries zeros, and copies $C800-$CFFF over the Lenslok's code at $C000 (03-build-and-load.md 3.7). The game
; then uses $C000-$CFFF as the back buffer of the 3D view: the top two thirds of a screen in the screen's own layout,
; drawn there, copied to $4000 each frame. The bytes here are the image as the kickoff leaves it: the back buffer
; still holds what the loader put there.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

